fixed BT_reference(channel). Then for all 38000 training profiles
(their own actual, varying view angle/CO2/etc.), the target becomes:

    btTargetResidual = btRaw - BT_reference;   % BT_reference broadcasts across all samples

The network still receives the profile's real view angle, CO2, etc. as
inputs — it's not being asked to ignore those, just to predict the
deviation from one fixed, well-known baseline state rather than the
full absolute radiance level from scratch. Since much of the absolute
